## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to design a DP for a non-standard segment value (length times segment max) with exact-k partitioning and path reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- 2D DP: dp[i][t] stores best value for first i elements using t segments
- Transition: dp[i][t] = max over j of dp[j][t-1] + (i-j) * max(A[j+1..i])
- On-the-fly max: as j decreases, update max(A[j+1..i]) incrementally
- Reconstruction: parent[i][t] stores last cut; backtrack to produce segments
- Complexity: O(n^2 k) time, O(nk) space

## Code Example
```javascript
function solve(A, n, k){
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const par = Array.from({length: n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let t=1;t<=Math.min(i,k);t++){
      let maxv = -Infinity;
      for(let j=i-1;j>=t-1;j--){
        maxv = Math.max(maxv, A[j]); // adjust if 0-based/1-based indexing
        const val = dp[j][t-1] + (i-j) * maxv;
        if(val > dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t] = val; par[i][t] = j; }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruct
  let segments = [];
  let i=n, t=k;
  while(t>0){
    const j = par[i][t];
    segments.push([j+1, i]);
    i = j; t--;
  }
  segments.reverse();
  return {value: dp[n][k], segments};
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Explores a new DP angle: selecting exactly k non-overlapping substrings with a per-substring palindrome-anagram constraint, requiring fast feasibility testing via prefix masks and reconstruction.

## Key Concepts

- Palindromable substrings via 26-bit parity mask
- Prefix XOR to test s[l..r] in O(1)
- DP over i and t with transitions from p-1
- Backpointer reconstruction; space optimization with rolling arrays
- Time complexity: O(n^2 k)

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxLenPalAnagram(s, k) {
  const n = s.length;
  const pref = new Array(n + 1).fill(0);
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) pref[i] = pref[i - 1] ^ (1 << (s.charCodeAt(i - 1) - 97));
  function popcount(x) { let c = 0; while (x) { x &= x - 1; c++; } return c; }
  function canPal(l, r) {
    return popcount(pref[r] ^ pref[l - 1]) <= 1;
  }
  // DP skeleton: dp[i][t] = max total length through i with t substrings
}
```

